s"} {:he "צ״ח", :translit "tishemonah", :gloss "ninety-eight"} {:he "במשנה תורה", :translit "be-Mishneh Torah", :gloss "in Mishneh Torah"} {:he "קמ״ג", :translit "me'ah arba'im usheloshah", :gloss "one hundred forty-three"} {:he "ערכין", :translit "archin", :gloss "valuations"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 90, :occurrences ["מתחלת התוכחה עד געלה נפשם"]} {:kind :other, :note "Word-count of 90 in Lev 26 passage matched to 90 years of the ten tribes' sin"} {:kind :other, :note "Valuation shekel totals (50+30+20+10+5+3+15+10 = 143) matched to 45 curses in Prophets + 98 in Mishneh Torah = 143"} {:kind :other, :note "Spelling variation between Chronicles (ליצחק) and Psalms (לישחק) read as basis for divine oath limiting exile"}], :frame {:text "The verse 'brimstone and salt, a burning… all the land' (Deuteronomy 29:22) describes the desolation of the Land of Israel. The ten tribes of the northern kingdom were exiled by Assyria after sinning throughout the period of their kingdom. Leviticus 26:40 employs the hitpa'el form והתוודו, matching its appearance in Ezra 10:1, which concerns confession. The catalog of valuation amounts in Leviticus 27:3–7 (fifty shekels for a male twenty to sixty, thirty for a female, etc.) follows immediately after the rebuke passage of Leviticus 26. Deuteronomy 28 contains a series of curses (the לוי section) numbering ninety-eight in standard rabbinic count.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 29:22" "2 Kings 17:6" "Leviticus 26:40" "Ezra 10:1" "Leviticus 27:3–7" "Deuteronomy 28"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 90, :occurrences ["מתחלת התוכחה עד געלה נפשם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "מתחלת התוכחה עד געלה נפשם", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Word-count of 90 in Lev 26 passage matched to 90 years of the ten tribes' sin", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Valuation shekel totals (50+30+20+10+5+3+15+10 = 143) matched to 45 curses in Prophets + 98 in Mishneh Torah = 143", :by :selah, :ran